  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1232 AM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nThough our dry weather lasts through Wednesday, the upper pattern is \nexpected to shift towards a more amplified western trof, eastern \nridge in the CONUS by Wednesday. This will lead to a few periods of \nrainfall chances in the extended forecast. The first is a warm \nadvection band of showers possible late Wednesday night and Thursday \nmorning. This is a low confidence, low POP forecast at this time, \nrepresented by 10-20% rainfall chances, and zero QPF at the \nmoment. \n\nThere is now enough signal for a short wave ridge in the area \nThursday afternoon and night that the NBM has removed the low POPs \nthat were previously there. The upper trof is then expected to see \nmore energy lift out towards Friday and Saturday with rain chances \nin the 25-80%. This seems to be heavily influenced by the bullish \nECMWF output in the model blend, but is also shown in some GFS ens \nmembers. Regardless of these pops, this late week forecast remains \nwell above normal, with highs in the 60s, lows in the 45-52 range \nand several days of breezy southwest winds.",
